WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:17.373
A gradual rollout limits how many devices receive an update at
once, so you can check results before continuing. Cohorts are
batches. Creation alone starts no devices, and you return to
approve further progress. Choose Rollouts in the sidebar to
release in stages.

2
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:24.373
Open Create a gradual rollout. Choose the published version and
matching device platform from your library.

3
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:32.995
A cohort is a batch of devices. Add named devices or groups to
the first batch; a device belongs to only one batch.

4
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:42.125
Set the pacing, observation period and failure threshold, then
review the exact plan. Creating a rollout does not start any
device.

5
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.384
Select the rollout, then admit the first devices after checking
device health.

6
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:57.443
This plan is created with devices waiting, not installed. Only
admit devices after reporting is configured and current signed
health is available.

7
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:07.056
Pause stops new devices from starting; it does not undo an
update already allowed to start. This example deliberately
admits no devices.

8
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:19.749
The saved plan is paused. Return after reporting is ready to
resume and explicitly approve the next batch. This clip does not
demonstrate a healthy rollout or automatic advancement.
